<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      strategy_defaults row for Strategy 6 (STRATEGIES.md, "Strategy 6").

      Why a changeset and not an operator INSERT
      ==========================================
      Strategy 6 is Strategy 2 plus three entry gates, and its measured edge
      (STRATEGY_ANALYSIS_TODO.md S27) was replayed on the SAME strategy_defaults
      block strategy 1 runs on - transaction_type SELL, the same max_loss,
      no_of_trades and no_of_parallel_trades. Every knob change tried on top
      (no_of_trades 2, 5-minute-only rules, SMA-200 dropped, premium floor 100)
      made it worse, because the gates already remove the trades those knobs
      remove and then some. So the block is not a decision left to whoever types
      the INSERT: it is "whatever strategy 1 has", copied - which also means the
      two strategies share ONE generated config row (configSignature) and appear
      as "1,6" on it, exactly the shape the replay measured.

      What it does NOT do
      ===================
      It does not tag strategy 6 on any sma_downtrend_rule, so nothing trades
      until an operator says so (CLAUDE.md Rule 0(c)). Switching it on is one
      row per rule:

          INSERT INTO sma_downtrend_rule_strategy (rule_id, strategy_id, enabled)
          SELECT rs.rule_id, 6, TRUE
            FROM sma_downtrend_rule_strategy rs
           WHERE rs.strategy_id = 1 AND rs.enabled = TRUE;

      Idempotent and order-safe: a no-op when strategy 6 already has a row, and
      a no-op on a database that has no strategy 1 row yet (fresh install before
      the operator seeds strategy 1 - then insert 6 by hand the same way, see
      docs/EOD_DOWNTREND.md "strategy_defaults"). opposite_side is FALSE: like 1
      and 2 it sells the leg the downtrend was detected on. target_mode /
      sl_mode (changeset 041) are copied too, so 6 brackets exactly as 1 does.
    -->
    <changeSet id="046_seed_strategy6_defaults" author="moneymaker">
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO strategy_defaults
                (strategy_id, transaction_type, lot_quantity, max_loss,
                 no_of_trades, no_of_parallel_trades, auto_config_enabled, opposite_side,
                 target_mode, sl_mode)
            SELECT 6, s.transaction_type, s.lot_quantity, s.max_loss,
                   s.no_of_trades, s.no_of_parallel_trades, s.auto_config_enabled, FALSE,
                   s.target_mode, s.sl_mode
              FROM strategy_defaults s
             WHERE s.strategy_id = 1
               AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM strategy_defaults x WHERE x.strategy_id = 6)
        </sql>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
